The TypeScript adaptation restricts negotiation to bounded linear graphs and
fourteen eight-bit layouts, uses shared candidate groups, adds explicit node
limits, and emits immutable conversion stages. The upstream source is available
in the pinned upstream/ffmpeg submodule. This notice does not assign a license to
the whole project or certify completion of the project-wide license audit.

format-pixel-format.ts adapts declared-format parsing and alias resolution from
FFmpeg libavfilter/vf_format.c and libavutil/pixdesc.c, with fixed numeric IDs from
libavutil/pixfmt.h at the same pinned commit. Copyright (c) 2007 Bobby Bingham;
Copyright (c) 2009 Michael Niedermayer <michaelni@gmx.at>.

This component is LGPL-2.1-or-later under LICENSES/LGPL-2.1-or-later.txt.
The TypeScript adaptation bounds saturated LP64/base-zero parsing, models signed32
enum storage, normalizes the fourteen declared layouts and fixed LE/gray aliases,
and retains duplicate validation and graph preflight. The surrounding linear
option parser follows the ASCII whitespace rules observed in graphparser.c,
libavutil/opt.c and avstring.c. General graph quoting and options are incomplete.

video-syntax.ts and video-parse.ts adapt token/option parsing and scoped scale
initialization from FFmpeg libavutil/avstring.c, libavutil/opt.c,
libavfilter/avfilter.c, graphparser.c and vf_scale.c at the same pinned commit.

