The TypeScript adaptation bounds single-path graphs, applies independent
quoting layers and protected whitespace, resolves final string options before
validation, and retains positive constant dimensions/default bicubic scope.
General graphs, expressions and additional options remain incomplete.

video-graph.ts adapts single-input/output pad linking from FFmpeg
libavfilter/graphparser.c at the pinned commit above.
Copyright (c) 2007 Bobby Bingham
Copyright (c) 2008 Vitor Sessak
Licensed LGPL-2.1-or-later under LICENSES/LGPL-2.1-or-later.txt.
The adaptation bounds graphs to 32 single-pad nodes and one connected path,
preserves declaration order for format queries, and exposes immutable metadata.
Branching, multiple inputs/outputs and general graph commands remain incomplete.

video-transpose.ts adapts plane transposition and direction/passthrough semantics
from FFmpeg libavfilter/vf_transpose.c at commit
946fcce07b6dcd0331c8cc609192aeff5e1924f8.
Copyright (c) 2010 Stefano Sabatini
Copyright (c) 2008 Vitor Sessak
LGPL-2.1-or-later; license text: LICENSES/LGPL-2.1-or-later.txt.
The TypeScript adaptation materializes tight positive strides, validates budgets
and source storage, and restricts direct operations to thirteen eight-bit layouts
with symmetric chroma. Negative-stride inputs and full frame-property semantics
remain incomplete. Graph format restrictions and legacy passthrough semantics
also follow vf_transpose.c. Internal input-trim registration placement follows
fftools/ffmpeg_filter.c at the same pinned commit (LGPL-2.1-or-later).

filter-topology.ts adapts libavfilter/graphparser.c pad linking at the same pinned
commit. Copyright (c) 2007 Bobby Bingham; Copyright (c) 2008 Vitor Sessak.
It adds bounded registry descriptors, immutable topology snapshots and a separate
DAG execution ordering check while preserving structural cyclic links.
video-graph-formats.ts extends the format-set negotiation adaptation described
above to bounded split branches, sink constraints and per-output sizes.
Both adaptations use LGPL-2.1-or-later and the accompanying license text.

video-stack.ts adapts plane placement and frame construction from
libavfilter/vf_stack.c at the same pinned commit.
Copyright (c) 2015 Paul B. Mahol.
The LGPL-2.1-or-later adaptation uses tight owned output storage, validates
synchronized timestamps, clips the final visible chroma boundary and rejects
overlapping Native parallel chroma writes before allocation.

frame-sync.ts adapts all-input state transitions and clock selection from
libavfilter/framesync.c and libavutil/rational.c at the pinned commit.
Copyright (c) 2013 Nicolas George.
Copyright (c) 2003 Michael Niedermayer <michaelni@gmx.at>.
It retains LGPL-2.1-or-later and the accompanying license text. The adaptation
uses bounded retention leases, exact bigint rescaling, explicit cancellation and
Native unreduced rational representations. Main/secondary and nearest modes are
not implemented. video-filter-graph.ts uses this clock selection for local joins.
video-stream.ts is independently authored replay/scheduling glue using these
components; this notice does not assign a license to the whole project or
complete the project-wide license audit.

